.TH WERKMEISTER-WORKSPACE-ABANDON 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-workspace\-abandon \- End a workspace without shipping: record the reason in closeout.md and the PR files, push every branch and keep them, remove the workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister workspace abandon\fR <reason> [name]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y, \-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-postmortem <reason>\fR
Close out without a post\-mortem; the reason goes in closeout.md
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The one way to end a workspace. First the post\-mortem: it refuses without \fBpostmortem.md\fR unless \fB\-\-skip\-postmortem\fR gives a reason. After every PR shipped, it closes the issue, writes \fBcloseout.md\fR, removes the workspace and deletes merged branches. \fBwerkmeister workspace abandon "<reason>"\fR instead records the reason, leaves the issue, pushes every branch and keeps them, and removes the workspace. It lists terminal Claude sessions still open in the workspace.
.PP
The full process is in docs/workspace\-lifecycle.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister workspace close
werkmeister workspace abandon "superseded by SW\-200" my\-feature
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
